    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • SRT Performance Joins the 2026 SEMA Show Featuring the First-Ever Jeep Wrangler Scrambler Concept\nWant To Drift an AMG? This Florida Motor Club Has Your Back, and You Can Bring the Family, Too\n18 photos\nPhoto: P1 Motor Club\nThere is a private motor club in Florida where Mercedes-AMG models are now standard-issue track cars for resident members. That arrangement is the result of a new partnership between P1 Motor Club and Mercedes-Benz USA, which officially makes Mercedes-Benz and its AMG performance division the Official Automotive Partner of the 650-acre (263-hectare) motorsports facility located in Port St. Lucie.\nThe German automaker will establish a permanent vehicle and operational presence across the Florida property. Through the deal, Mercedes-Benz USA will supply the venue with an ongoing fleet of Mercedes-Benz and Mercedes-AMG vehicles spanning high-performance sports cars, standard luxury passenger models, off-road utilities, and commercial Sprinter vans to support daily operations across the site.\nP1 Motor Club plans to deploy this manufacturer-backed fleet across several internal departments, covering track driving sessions, guest hospitality, member transportation, and day-to-day logistics. Within that supplied lineup, Mercedes-AMG models are slated to serve as the primary street-car rentals for club-managed members, visiting guests, and corporate driving groups booking track time at the motorsports complex.\nBeyond basic track rentals, the supplied vehicles will be integrated directly into P1 Motor Club's internal instructional programs. The fleet will support the facility's high-performance driving and racing schools, off-road and rally courses, and general driver coaching. This allows members and guests to use factory-supplied cars across the club's various asphalt and loose-surface training areas instead of relying solely on personal vehicles.\nPhoto: P1 Motor Club In addition to supplying cars, the agreement designates the Port St. Lucie venue as a primary United States operating base for select AMG Experience driving programs and brand activations. In other words, when a new Mercedes or AMG model breaks ground (from the most savage hypercars and supercars to the humblest daily drivers), the P1 Motor Club members will get their hands on them before regular customers.\nThis brings the automaker's complete factory driving academy—consisting of the Performance, Advanced, Pro, Pro+, Drift, and Drift+ training courses—directly to the Florida venue for both novice drivers and experienced track enthusiasts.\nThese factory-run courses will operate alongside P1 Motor Club's existing in-house curriculum, which already includes racing schools, drift instruction, rallycross sessions, karting programs, and private coaching. Mercedes-Benz USA also plans to set up dedicated AMG-branded facilities on the campus and use the property's track infrastructure to host recurring customer drive events and official brand activations throughout the year for invited drivers.\nPhoto: P1 Motor Club Aurora Straus, a Founding Partner of P1 Motor Club and a professional racing driver who competes in Mercedes-AMG machinery on race weekends, said the partnership is designed to integrate the automaker into the daily routine of the club. According to Straus, placing the brand in the garages, classrooms, and racetracks gives members and their families direct access to the company's vehicles and instruction.\nLocated on Florida's Treasure Coast about 45 minutes north of Palm Beach, P1 Motor Club contains more than 9 miles (14.5 kilometers) of private tracks, including a 4.5-mile (7.2-kilometer) FIA Grade 2 circuit, a 3-mile (4.8-kilometer) secondary course, and karting, drift, and rally layouts. The invitation-only club also features garage townhomes, residences, and a clubhouse for Charter License holders.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nAMG mercedes-menz P1 motor club motor club Drift School driving school\nAbout the author: Razvan Calin\nAfter nearly two decades in news television, Răzvan turned to a different medium. He’s been a field journalist, a TV producer, and a seafarer but found that he feels right at home among petrolheads. Full profile\nUP NEXT Toyota China Recalls Land Cruiser Prado Hybrid and Lexus GX 550h for Potential Fuel Leak",
